    ]
  },
  "summary": {
    "en": [
      "Richard Fleischman shaped Cleveland architecture through more than 480 projects, over 120 awards, and a design philosophy he described as sculpted space. His work included churches, civic buildings, reused structures, furniture, planning, and sculpture, while his teaching and professional leadership connected Hungarian heritage, design education, and regional civic life."
    ]
